  PART 3: FAST FORMULAS

  c3 is computable in O(n^3) directly:
  For each triple (i,j,k): check if A[i][j]*A[j][k]*A[k][i] + A[i][k]*A[k][j]*A[j][i] > 0
  OR: c3 = C(n,3) - sum_v C(s_v, 2) = C(n,3) - (S_2 - C(n,2))/2
  This second formula is O(n) given scores!

  S_2 = sum s_v^2 is O(n) from the score sequence.
  So c3 is O(n) from scores. No need to enumerate triples.

  H at n <= 4: H = 1 + 2*C(n,3) + C(n,2) - S_2.
  This is O(n) from the score sequence alone.

  PART 4: FORMULA AT n=6

  At n=6: alpha_2 = #{complementary triple pairs where both are 3-cycles}
  (Because disjoint 3+5 needs 8 > 6 vertices, impossible.)

  MISMATCH: H=15, formula=11, c3=4, c5=1, a2=0, S2=47
  MISMATCH: H=13, formula=11, c3=4, c5=1, a2=0, S2=47
